  "title": "Diagnostics export, trait detection and the threat note (NFR-07, QLT-11, QLT-13)",
  "body": "Builds three Musts that had no test, under the owner's direction to drop process gates and finish today. Feature-spec review and sign-off were waived; the simplifications below are disclosed instead.\n\n- **NFR-07**: `inspect --view export` returns a redacted diagnostics projection as a preview. Saving is cooperative: the kernel writes nothing (option B of the local spec).\n- **QLT-11**: static path and dependency signals for the R1 traits. Partial coverage everywhere, so results are `present` or `unknown`. `decide traits` records project traits and takes corrections; change traits are recorded at each check. Not built: a missed-trait finding type, lane raises from late change traits, and trait obligations.\n- **QLT-13**: `threat`-tagged basis elements; `threat-note-open` blocks `checked-local` for a present security trait without a complete note. An `unknown` trait does not require the note, and an actor may be a constraint.\n\nNothing is observed on the real host.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
